    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW21i51nf5mHWex3PPP3SRwVN)_\n\n## Summary\nNew \"Linting the .bib files\" section in `sp-bibprocess` (doc `sp-academic.org`, tangled to `sp-bibprocess.el`). Independent of #230.\n\n- `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-report` (`C-c w b l`): dry run over `sp-bibtex-files`. Reports `author`/`editor` names not in the canonical `Last, First` form, fields out of the order of `sp-bibtex-field-order`, duplicate keys, entries it cannot read, and names one typo (≤2 edits) away from an existing author note.\n- `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-apply` (`C-c w b L`): asks once, copies each file to `sp-bibtex-lint-backup-directory`, rewrites names and field order. Duplicates and typo hints are not changed. An entry with a `%` comment inside is never rewritten (it is reported).\n- `sp-bibtex-author-capf` in `bibtex-mode`: completes names in `author`/`editor` from the author notes, in `Last, First`.\n- **No author note is ever created**; the vault is only read. A name with no note is not reported.\n- Runs in slices through `sp-async-work` (100 entries per slice).\n\n## Decisions for you\n- Default `sp-bibtex-field-order` is my guess (author, editor, title … year, doi, url, file, keywords, abstract, note); please adjust.\n- A rewritten entry is regenerated as `@type{key,` with fields aligned at `=`; values keep their text and delimiters.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] ERT `tests/sp-bibprocess-lint-test.el` on Emacs 29.3: 6 pass (names, fields, typo hint, report+apply with backup, comment entry untouched, completion).\n- [x] Synthetic 40,000-entry `.bib` with 3,000 author notes, every entry flagged: 24 s in slices.\n- [ ] Not run: your real `.bib` files. Run `sp-bibtex-lint-report` first and read it before `-apply`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9HDQBXXdZ9XpEdeVx)_",
